{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== 26/26 GREEN. J11 IS COMPLETE — BOTH DIRECTIONS OF THE EPIC'S HEADLINE AC ARE PROVEN LIVE. ===\n\nRUN: GitHub Actions 30718360110, job 91417809065 (\"jira DC harness smoke (real Jira Data Center,\nephemeral)\"), main @ 96b82de1e0 (which is change 1177 merged). Result:\n\n    26 passed in 535.13s (0:08:55)\n\nZero failures, zero skips. This is the first fully green DC harness run in epic e369.\n\nWHAT THE PREVIOUS RUN LEFT OPEN IS NOW CLOSED. Run 30716856124 was 25/26; its single failure was\n`test_the_store_copy_is_complete_and_scrubbed`, asserting a copied set containing `.ensure-*` marker\ndot-files against a baseline set that did not. Change 1177 (\"count tickets structurally, pin the\nbaseline\") repaired exactly that — filter store entries STRUCTURALLY instead of by an enumerated\ndot-file list, and pin the baseline commit rather than re-sampling a LIVE tickets branch at assertion\ntime. That cell now PASSES, and it was the only red.\n\nTHE TWO CELLS THAT CARRY THE EPIC'S HEADLINE, both green in this run:\n  PASSED test_store_copy_isolation.py::test_a_dc_issue_reaches_the_local_store_inbound\n  PASSED test_store_copy_isolation.py::test_a_local_edit_reaches_the_dc_issue_outbound\ni.e. \"an issue created in DC appears locally\" AND \"a local edit appears in DC\", both against a real\nData Center instance, over a complete scrubbed copy of the real production store. The outbound half\nhad never had evidence before this story; the analysis of why its GREEN carries information (unique\nwritten value, read back from the instance, binding asserted by the fixture before yielding) is in\nthe preceding comment on this ticket and is unchanged by this run.\n\nTHE OTHER 24, for the record: 4 harness-smoke (Server deployment at the pinned 8.x, PAT bearer auth,\nbogus token rejected, REST v2 round-trip); 3 reconcile-pass (shared jira provenance on a DC-created\nticket, a repeated pass writes nothing, no unhandled exception); 4 more store-copy-isolation\n(isolation of BOTH repos, complete+scrubbed copy, inbound create PLANNED, zero deletions and zero\noutbound updates); 11 transport (create/get/update/transition round-trip, resolve by immutable\nnumeric id, rekeyed issue, deleted issue fails by key AND id, probe classification, comment/search\nshapes, labels+links, authoritative user search, unknown assignee raises, unavailable transition\nraises, backend selection); 2 user-guide (the documented config and dry-run work; the documented\nsetup refuses a PAT from config).\n\nONE UNRELATED JOB IN THE SAME RUN IS RED, AND IT IS NOT THIS EPIC'S — checked rather than waved off.\nJob 91417809053 \"external integration (live services)\" reports 2 failed / 26 passed:\n`test_execution_mode_live.py::test_single_turn_live_structured_output` and\n`test_workflow_live.py::test_live_plan_review_workflow_engine_produces_real_verdict`. Both are LLM\nlive-service tests with no Jira or Data Center involvement, and the SAME job failed in the previous\nrun (30716856124) before any of this story's code existed. Pre-existing, and outside e369's scope."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785619793836688001,"uuid":"e7872709-4f43-4d21-a731-ee271ec1057a"}